{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/1099466-abyssal-awareness-charms","id":1099466,"title":"Abyssal Awareness Charms","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted","Abyssal Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-06-02T05:41:57-07:00","id":1099466,"title":"Abyssal Awareness Charms","content":"<span style=\"font-size:14px\">I am currently working on Abyssal charms for a homebrew conversion. Most recently, I have been pondering Awareness charms. Solar awareness covers three main areas - Stealth &amp; Surprise Nixing, Sense-expansion and Tracking. I've tried to address the same areas using these charms with (hopefully) some success. I'm hoping for some constructive criticism about these charms so that I can do a good job on them. There are only 18 charms, so the coverage isn't as detailed as the solar tree; this is a deliberate step - a taste of the charms that I can develop later on if needed. <br /> <br /> I'm specifically looking for feedback in the following areas:</span><ul><li><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Are the charms thematically sound? Do they look/feel/sound like abyssal charms?</span></li> <li><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Are the mote costs in the right sort of region? Have I under/over estimated the cost of charms?</span></li> <li><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Is there a deficiency that needs addressing in coverage? Have I missed an important use of an ability in the charm tree?</span></li> <li><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Are they cool? </span></li> </ul><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Here is the link: <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1l3oUDcuALxEJBAwjRW4pTDfcp1LRdgZBbnxFL5Y1mgg/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Abyssal Awareness Charms</a><br /> <br /> Thanks in Advance!</span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13409-klaymore","name":"Klaymore","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13409_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-03T11:16:02-07:00","id":1099862,"title":"","content":"Some of the ideas here seem really cool to me. I'm not the best personally at costings and balance but you look like you're on to some really solid thematics with charms like Siakal's Scent, Tick of the Fragile Clock and the ones that interact with ghosts. You've managed to play into the abyssal wheel house and avoid simply aping solars too much which is nice to see.<br /> <br /> My biggest nitpick would be that recreating a scene like with Undying Oracle, or working out the cause of death with Void Stares Back (I'm a fan of the rest of that charm) seem a little more like Investigation than Awareness. It might be worth taking another pass and either justifying to yourself why some of these charms are one and not the other, or tweaking them to be less Investigation-like.<br /> <br /> Have you considered charms based around fetters, locations or other such things? Charms to allow an abyssal to have a sense of who is moving around their creepy castle or crypt. Or to be aware when someone interferes with the keepsake they have of the person who allowed them to resist the call of the void and take the exaltation offered to them. There's a certain amount of thematic gothic potential to be played with there you might want to toy with.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13512-andrix","name":"andrix","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13512_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"28"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-03T11:46:25-07:00","id":1099870,"title":"","content":"My thought is charms based around passionate feelings (aka Intimacies). When someone speaks your name with great anger, great hate, great love, you can FEEL their regard and hone in on their feelings towards you so you can sense them. And then there's all the things you could do around your own Intimacies.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr />\u200bWhen noise turns to silence, when colors dull and pale, when reality no longer makes sense, there shall you find me. There, in the dreams of the River of Faceless Millions, do I dwell.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://harenm.deviantart.com/gallery/\" target=\"_blank\">http://harenm.deviantart.com/gallery/</a> for my art.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/378-haren","name":"haren","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar378_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"664"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-05T07:08:43-07:00","id":1100432,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>andrix</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/1099466-abyssal-awareness-charms?p=1099862#post1099862\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Some of the ideas here seem really cool to me. I'm not the best personally at costings and balance but you look like you're on to some really solid thematics with charms like Siakal's Scent, Tick of the Fragile Clock and the ones that interact with ghosts. You've managed to play into the abyssal wheel house and avoid simply aping solars too much which is nice to see.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thank you! It is nice to know that I have some consensus on the approach I'm taking. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>andrix</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/1099466-abyssal-awareness-charms?p=1099862#post1099862\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My biggest nitpick would be that recreating a scene like with Undying Oracle, or working out the cause of death with Void Stares Back (I'm a fan of the rest of that charm) seem a little more like Investigation than Awareness. It might be worth taking another pass and either justifying to yourself why some of these charms are one and not the other, or tweaking them to be less Investigation-like.</div> </div> </div> </div>I suspect you could well be right. When it comes to writing the Investigation charms, there may well be some adjustments and changes made to these charms if they fit a wheelhouse better. I'm currently working on the Bureaucracy charms at the moment and skipping brawl until I get to melee (so, some time to go yet).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>andrix</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/1099466-abyssal-awareness-charms?p=1099862#post1099862\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Have you considered charms based around fetters, locations or other such things? Charms to allow an abyssal to have a sense of who is moving around their creepy castle or crypt. Or to be aware when someone interferes with the keepsake they have of the person who allowed them to resist the call of the void and take the exaltation offered to them. There's a certain amount of thematic gothic potential to be played with there you might want to toy with.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes. Specifically, I have considered them in regards to links with groups / kingdoms / factions within the underworld and how the Abyssals could form their own organisations of ghosts fettered to their leader or to an ideal or such. As far as I understand ghosts in 3e, however, fetters are intimacies for ghosts. Removing fetters sends the ghost off to lethe or Oblivion. Without more information though, I cant be sure how strong this is. When ghosts are developed further in official sources, I can adjust charms to suit, or craft new ones. <br /> <br /> If you have a specific idea for a gothic charm, I would simply LOVE to include it in the charm set. I'd rather have a broad, deep, fuller charm set written from the capital of many authors than simply my own charms limited by my own imagination.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13409-klaymore","name":"Klaymore","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13409_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-05T07:10:58-07:00","id":1100434,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>haren</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/1099466-abyssal-awareness-charms?p=1099870#post1099870\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My thought is charms based around passionate feelings (aka Intimacies). When someone speaks your name with great anger, great hate, great love, you can FEEL their regard and hone in on their feelings towards you so you can sense them. And then there's all the things you could do around your own Intimacies.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I love this idea. In the Solar Charm sets, this sort of sense usually comes under the ability most representitive of the actions you might take in response to such things. In Bureaucracy, for example, solars can sense thefts in the markets they inhabit. I definatly could use some of these ideas in the charm sets for the Abyssals though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13409-klaymore","name":"Klaymore","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13409_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-05T07:15:57-07:00","id":1100437,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Klaymore</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/1099466-abyssal-awareness-charms?p=1100434#post1100434\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> I love this idea. In the Solar Charm sets, this sort of sense usually comes under the ability most representitive of the actions you might take in response to such things. In Bureaucracy, for example, solars can sense thefts in the markets they inhabit. I definatly could use some of these ideas in the charm sets for the Abyssals though.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, I really like Abyssals, but I wasn't trying to influence you too much, since I've done a bit on my own charm ideas for Abyssals (Though I've been focusing on Performance first). It's why I tried to keep mine short and not too detailed (rather than a lack of interest on my part, because I liked these!)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr />\u200bWhen noise turns to silence, when colors dull and pale, when reality no longer makes sense, there shall you find me. There, in the dreams of the River of Faceless Millions, do I dwell.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://harenm.deviantart.com/gallery/\" target=\"_blank\">http://harenm.deviantart.com/gallery/</a> for my art.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/378-haren","name":"haren","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar378_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"664"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-07T14:02:09-07:00","id":1101361,"title":"","content":"Tick of the Fragile Clock -- excellent, except that the language excludes detecting the Exalted. I love the idea that Abyssals should be incredibly sensitive to the sound of living creatures being alive.<br /> <br /> Siaka's Scent -- excellent; the Abyssal Exalted have far more reason to be sensitive to the presence of blood than even the Lunar Exalted<br /> <br /> Adder's Tongue -- cool<br /> <br /> <br /> Shroudsight -- I like the idea that Abyssal Exalted &quot;hunger for sensation&quot; as justification for their perception Charms.<br /> <br /> <br /> Ripples of the Dead -- Occult tends to be the Ability for detecting spirits, but I like how this Charm compares to Spirit-Detecting Glance.<br /> <br /> Stolen Sight Technique, Ancestor Army Awareness, Dead Gods See All -- similar concerns<br /> <br /> <br /> Void Stares Back, Undying Oracle Meditation -- a bit too much Investigation in these Charms, but cool.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-07T18:57:42-07:00","id":1101453,"title":"","content":"Sleep. Perhaps Abyssal Exalted should be able to take their sense of death and dying and extend it to the &quot;lesser death&quot; of sleep. The Neverborn are forever sleeping in death, and mortal ghosts could be considered sleeping in between periods of being &quot;awake&quot; (alive).<br /> <br /> Besides, being able to detect people when they're asleep is an amazing way to make the Abyssal Exalted more scarily predatorial.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-08T14:37:20-07:00","id":1101742,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/1099466-abyssal-awareness-charms?p=1101361#post1101361\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Tick of the Fragile Clock -- excellent, except that the language excludes detecting the Exalted. I love the idea that Abyssals should be incredibly sensitive to the sound of living creatures being alive.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'll take a look at that and reword it, perhaps. Its meant to detect living things rather than mere mortals... Watch this space..<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/1099466-abyssal-awareness-charms?p=1101361#post1101361\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ripples of the Dead -- Occult tends to be the Ability for detecting spirits, but I like how this Charm compares to Spirit-Detecting Glance.<br /> Stolen Sight Technique, Ancestor Army Awareness, Dead Gods See All -- similar concerns</div> </div> </div> </div>And it still will be - But the Abyssals are more likely as a group to deal with ghosts on a regular basis and it seemed to me that knowing who is a ghost and who is alive, sensing necrotic energy and the faint whif of rotting flesh should all be 'senses' over occult understanding. Immaterial spirits cant be seen with any of these charms. Dealing with Gods, Demons and Elementals will will be done using Occult. Ghosts are just squarely in the Abyssals wheelhouse. <br /> <br /> [<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/1099466-abyssal-awareness-charms?p=1101361#post1101361\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Void Stares Back, Undying Oracle Meditation -- a bit too much Investigation in these Charms, but cool.</div> </div> </div> </div>Seems a popular view - I'll review where these fit when i come to write the investigation charm set. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13409-klaymore","name":"Klaymore","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13409_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-08T14:42:09-07:00","id":1101747,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/1099466-abyssal-awareness-charms?p=1101453#post1101453\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sleep. Perhaps Abyssal Exalted should be able to take their sense of death and dying and extend it to the &quot;lesser death&quot; of sleep. The Neverborn are forever sleeping in death, and mortal ghosts could be considered sleeping in between periods of being &quot;awake&quot; (alive).<br /> <br /> Besides, being able to detect people when they're asleep is an amazing way to make the Abyssal Exalted more scarily predatorial.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Sleep always seems to suggest Wyld energies to me, despite the fact that there are demons that inhabit dreams (the Sigil's Dreamer and the Demon form the jumpstart). I like the idea of being able to sense 'helpless' victims though. Its very 'vampiric' - I can imagine one of Death's Champions sneaking into a house to take the life of his sleeping victim... I'll ponder it! Thanks for the idea.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13409-klaymore","name":"Klaymore","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13409_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-11T07:23:25-07:00","id":1102500,"title":"","content":"I don't mean to go too far off the feedback path, but could you possibly share the rest of the charms you've worked on so far (not just the awareness)? I'd def. like to check them out! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> Keep up the good work!!!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11633-thesly9","name":"TheSly9","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11633_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"79"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-11T07:38:52-07:00","id":1102502,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheSly9</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/1099466-abyssal-awareness-charms?p=1102500#post1102500\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't mean to go too far off the feedback path, but could you possibly share the rest of the charms you've worked on so far (not just the awareness)? I'd def. like to check them out! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> Keep up the good work!!!</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I've done<br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1HwWbe1c5ET_z9YlkoRydwsdStQ4Uv2QWvWFRebz3mv8/edit\" target=\"_blank\">ARCHERY</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1U7J77B0MF_wEF673rHVeifKiDQVm3mQp1k5WWK0fEoQ/edit\" target=\"_blank\">ATHLETICS</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1l3oUDcuALxEJBAwjRW4pTDfcp1LRdgZBbnxFL5Y1mgg/edit\" target=\"_blank\">AWARENESS</a><br /> and I'm currently working on Bureaucracy charms too. <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13409-klaymore","name":"Klaymore","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13409_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-12T07:25:52-07:00","id":1102800,"title":"","content":"Thanks for sharing! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Are you just going to be doing the charms? Or will you be doing a complete Abyssal home-brew splat? If the latter, I was wondering what you will do for the resonance system. Will you keep it or something like it? Or do you have something else in mind?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11633-thesly9","name":"TheSly9","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11633_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"79"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-12T08:12:10-07:00","id":1102817,"title":"","content":"My intent is to complete a home-brew of the entire splat eventually. My thoughts on resonance are still somewhat nebulous though - In 2e, the device was a leash around the Abyssal's neck, killing off people that she had spent time developing relationships with. This isn't rewarding roleplay - but largely was damaging to it, I find. With Resonance, I want to change that. Instead of making the deathknight have a 'doom radiation sphere' around them, I want to empower roleplay. <br /> <br /> To this end, I thought of some rough ideas like<ul><li>Resonance twists realtionships, changing the intimacies others hold towards the abyssal. Love becomes obsession, annoyance becomes hatred. Friendship turns to paranoia. Mortals are very suseptible to these effects, while the exalted are less so.</li> <li>Bad things happen. People don't just fall down dead, but the Abyssal has some forewarning of how many will die that he cares about (Such as a mine collapse in town) and he knows its fated to happen - if he does nothing, can his intimacies stand so strong? If he acts, does he not cause the disaster he seeks to avoid?</li> </ul>As you can see, my ideas are very nebulous at this point. Any ideas?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13409-klaymore","name":"Klaymore","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13409_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-12T10:47:29-07:00","id":1102865,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Klaymore</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/1099466-abyssal-awareness-charms?p=1102817#post1102817\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My intent is to complete a home-brew of the entire splat eventually. My thoughts on resonance are still somewhat nebulous though - In 2e, the device was a leash around the Abyssal's neck, killing off people that she had spent time developing relationships with. This isn't rewarding roleplay - but largely was damaging to it, I find. With Resonance, I want to change that. Instead of making the deathknight have a 'doom radiation sphere' around them, I want to empower roleplay.<br /> <br /> To this end, I thought of some rough ideas like<ul><li>Resonance twists realtionships, changing the intimacies others hold towards the abyssal. Love becomes obsession, annoyance becomes hatred. Friendship turns to paranoia. Mortals are very suseptible to these effects, while the exalted are less so.</li> <li>Bad things happen. People don't just fall down dead, but the Abyssal has some forewarning of how many will die that he cares about (Such as a mine collapse in town) and he knows its fated to happen - if he does nothing, can his intimacies stand so strong? If he acts, does he not cause the disaster he seeks to avoid?</li> </ul>As you can see, my ideas are very nebulous at this point. Any ideas?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I ran an Abyssal PbP game a while back and it never made it far enough for us to us Resonance or to really use much in the way of charms. As such, we never really gave any hard thought into resonance as it was just one of those things where we were going to just figure it out when the situation came up. I don't have a good answer for you, but I will def. think about it and get back to you. I do like the first of your two concepts. That could def. work, methinks.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11633-thesly9","name":"TheSly9","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11633_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"79"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-16T08:18:06-07:00","id":1104301,"title":"","content":"Well, I haven't thought of anything crazy or awesome, but I did pitch it to the guys on the Exalted Discord to see what their ideas were. A fair number suggested using a similar system to the 3E Solar system for limit break/virtue flaws, but with the Abyssals it would be directly tied/associated with the concept &quot;Chivalry of Death&quot; which the 3E book talks about. Your ideas, after some minor molding, could even be added into to such a system.<br /> <br /> Someone also pointed out there is a lot of play room here as how one Abyssal who serves a Death Lord could be vastly different from how the next Abyssal serves his or her liege. For example, how someone serves the Mask of Winter is different than how someone who seeks to honor the First and Forgotten Lion would think/go about the &quot;Chivalry of Death&quot; concept. I'm not sure if that helps or not, but I thought it was a decent suggestion as the ground work for it mechanically is already present, you'd just need to change the triggers to give resonance and make sure they fall in line with the CoD concept.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11633-thesly9","name":"TheSly9","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11633_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"79"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}